Build fix, Windows: a Skia source file that is not in the build.

SkFont::makeStrikeRef() returns an SkStrikeRef, whose members are in
src/core/SkStrikeRef.cpp, and Skia's CMake file here does not list it.
Nothing calls makeStrikeRef(), so where a library may be linked with
symbols unresolved (Linux) nobody notices; a DLL may not be.

diff --git a/Source/ThirdParty/skia/CMakeLists.txt b/Source/ThirdParty/skia/CMakeLists.txt
index 49b926228..f050775a5 100644
--- a/Source/ThirdParty/skia/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Source/ThirdParty/skia/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -238,6 +238,7 @@ add_library(Skia STATIC
     src/core/SkStream.cpp
     src/core/SkStrike.cpp
     src/core/SkStrikeCache.cpp
+    src/core/SkStrikeRef.cpp
     src/core/SkStrikeSpec.cpp
     src/core/SkString.cpp
     src/core/SkStringUtils.cpp
